#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186242844 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "765ef63a-e3f0-503b-876d-3b4776b2cafe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Approximate Solutions to Exponential Equations Using the Natural Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05d2ae20-b1e6-53c2-8203-599899848b86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.792" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242846}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05d2ae20-b1e6-53c2-8203-599899848b86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.792" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242846} :answer-field/id #uuid "bef023fa-665d-5288-8b1a-01eadf984860" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242845}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b2ee8216-6d1d-59ed-ad9d-e2de4dc9dea5" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-228897" :question/problem "If ${e}^{x}=6,$ then $x≈${{field-1}}, rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, we take $ln$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x} & =6 \\\\ ln⁡({e}^{x}) & =ln⁡(6) \\\\ x & =ln⁡(6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx≈1.792\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186242847 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "765ef63a-e3f0-503b-876d-3b4776b2cafe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Approximate Solutions to Exponential Equations Using the Natural Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c9a635b-aaec-5ca8-97fc-9291250a923e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.732" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242849} {:answer/id #uuid "3c91e76d-c3a3-54da-ae5d-dc5e9c149d1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.197" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242850}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c9a635b-aaec-5ca8-97fc-9291250a923e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.732" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242849} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9c08d88-1e8e-589f-aba6-9061ff1cb5e6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242848}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a2647380-b90f-5a94-b8f2-387bb22f6b39" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-263077" :question/problem "If ${e}^{3x}=9,$ then $x≈${{field-1}}, rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, we take $ln$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3x} & =9 \\\\ ln⁡({e}^{3x}) & =ln⁡(9) \\\\ 3x & =ln⁡(9) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}ln⁡(9)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx≈0.732\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186242851 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "765ef63a-e3f0-503b-876d-3b4776b2cafe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Approximate Solutions to Exponential Equations Using the Natural Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed15ff26-098c-539f-b65f-ec0c6ef615d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9.222" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242853}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed15ff26-098c-539f-b65f-ec0c6ef615d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9.222" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242853} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b00f4e8-2a59-5368-91a6-0a4c4194237c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242852}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1d52d063-3aaf-5d01-981f-476f12121b24" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-263081" :question/problem "If ${e}^{5-y/2}=\\sqrt[5]{7},$ then $y≈${{field-1}}, rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, we take $ln$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5-y/2} & =\\sqrt[5]{7} \\\\ ln⁡({e}^{5-y/2}) & =ln⁡(\\sqrt[5]{7}) \\\\ 5-\\frac{y}{2} & =ln⁡({7}^{1/5})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power rule to the right-hand side and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5-\\frac{y}{2} & =\\frac{1}{5}ln⁡(7) \\\\ -\\frac{y}{2} & =\\frac{1}{5}ln⁡(7)-5 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{2}{5}ln⁡(7)+10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\ny≈9.222\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186242854 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "10095048-0db6-5b4e-889f-303f07449367" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Solutions to Exponential Equations when Rearrangement is Required"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c530ded5-7a6d-593d-9882-8064e7270cbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.403" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242856}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c530ded5-7a6d-593d-9882-8064e7270cbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.403" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242856} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cf168ad-9b88-5205-8c0b-1711ce4d2696" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242855}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cba7720d-211d-5524-a5d3-66ab503bec17" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-263199" :question/problem "If $9-{e}^{3-4x}=5,$ then $x≈${{field-1}}, rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9-{e}^{3-4x} & =5 \\\\ -{e}^{3-4x} & =5-9 \\\\ -{e}^{3-4x} & =-4 \\\\ {e}^{3-4x} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3-4x} & =4 \\\\ ln⁡({e}^{3-4x}) & =ln⁡(4) \\\\ 3-4x & =ln⁡(4) \\\\ -4x & =ln⁡(4)-3 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{4}ln⁡(4)+\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx≈0.403\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186242857 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "10095048-0db6-5b4e-889f-303f07449367" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Solutions to Exponential Equations when Rearrangement is Required"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f91be964-ec08-50fb-b369-57a2ab375e2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.554" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242859} {:answer/id #uuid "7aed4d88-0562-5615-8276-5cb34bf08c20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.277" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242860} {:answer/id #uuid "c3c3e5f8-5d80-5d42-8c9e-32284de6f3ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.277" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242861} {:answer/id #uuid "df298feb-ab33-5a76-b32d-4def12ca73d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.554" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242862} {:answer/id #uuid "7aa969f5-c918-5712-bf08-656d1501e115" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.727" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242863}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3c3e5f8-5d80-5d42-8c9e-32284de6f3ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.277" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242861} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ad74edb-40bd-5b93-b5ad-15850d4cbd3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242858}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3ef74d8c-cba1-50dc-af84-671391d39214" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-66902" :question/problem "Given that ${e}^{-5z}-6=-2,$ find the value of $z$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-5z}-6 & =-2 \\\\ {e}^{-5z} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-5z} & =4 \\\\ ln⁡({e}^{-5z}) & =ln⁡(4) \\\\ -5z & =ln⁡(4) \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{5}ln⁡(4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $z=-\\frac{1}{5}ln⁡(4)$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\nz≈-0.277\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}]}
